{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_352","type":"agent_message","text":"Implemented the S05 packet. Summary of what I did and verified.\n\n**Changes**\n- `docs/dev/harness-gap-closure/s05-credential-use-boundary.md` — ledger: source→policy→effect chain, coverage matrix, explicit residuals.\n- `tests/unit/provider-credential-use-boundary-ledger.test.ts` — guard test pinning the policy matrix, absence of credential-value inputs, the single call site, and residual recording.\n- `harness/specs/tasks/harness-gap-credential-use-boundary.md` — gateway-backend-communication task spec.\n- `docs/dev/harness-gap-closure/s05-acceptance.json` — agent-driven acceptance record (`driven_by: agent`, product locks unchanged).\n- `docs/dev/harness-gap-closure/S05-SHA256SUMS` — digests for the four artifacts above.\n\nThe gate is the existing `resolveProviderCredentialUsePolicy`, consulted only from `image-generate-tool.ts`'s explicit override branch; no second credential policy, no default/fallback/storage change. Denials occur before any credential read and the policy input/reason carry no credential value.\n\n**Checks Actually Run**\n- `node harness/src/cli.mjs validate --spec harness/specs/tasks/harness-gap-credential-use-boundary.md --no-diff` → `Spec is valid` (exit 0).\n- `node harness/src/cli.mjs validate --spec harness/specs/scenarios/gateway-backend-communication.md --no-diff` → valid (exit 0).\n- `harness run --dry-run` reconstructed offline (changed-path ownership + boundary scan) → `pass (dry-run)`, 0 failures, no uncovered/residual paths.\n- S05 ledger guard executed against this working tree with a local vitest-compatible shim → `4 passed, 0 failed`.\n- Policy matrix executed against this tree's real policy/provenance source → 18/18 assertions pass (trusted/no-override allowed; external/derived/missing confined to bound scope; denials restricted with credential-free reason).\n- Credential scan over the 5 files → 0 hits.\n- `S05-SHA256SUMS` read back and every entry matched; `s05-acceptance.json` parses and is agent-attributed.\n- `node scripts/check-no-bom.mjs` → ok (exit 0).\n\n**Notes**\n- `pnpm`/`vitest`/`tsgo`/`eslint`/comms scripts and `repo:test-coverage:check` could not run: no `node_modules`, no git repo in this sandbox (same at the pristine `base` checkout). Those gates are environmental, not task failures.\n- Two runtime tests declared in the spec's `requiredTests` (`openclaw_runtime/src/agents/tools/provider-credential-use-policy.test.ts`, `.../image-generate-tool.credential-use-provenance.test.ts`) are absent from this workspace (they exist at `baseCommit`); I did not add or touch them, per the instruction not to inspect or modify held-out oracle tests. The policy and call-site they target are unchanged, so their behavior is unaffected.\n- Pre-existing baseline red unrelated to this task: 7 sibling `harness-gap-*` specs lack `lifecycleStatus` (identical at `base`), and `verify-evidence-sha256sums.mjs` reports drift on unrelated earlier packets."}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_353","type":"command_execution","command":"\"D:\\\\software\\\\PowerShell\\\\pwsh-7.6.6\\\\pwsh.exe\" -Command \"Set-Content -Path \\\"D:\\\\tmp\\\\s05verify\\\\result.json\\\" -Value @'\n{\n  \\\"status\\\": \\\"completed\\\",\n  \\\"summary\\\": \\\"S05 credential-use boundary ledger implemented: added docs/dev/harness-gap-closure/s05-credential-use-boundary.md, tests/unit/provider-credential-use-boundary-ledger.test.ts, harness/specs/tasks/harness-gap-credential-use-boundary.md, docs/dev/harness-gap-closure/s05-acceptance.json (driven_by=agent, product locks unchanged) and docs/dev/harness-gap-closure/S05-SHA256SUMS. The ledger pins the existing resolveProviderCredentialUsePolicy gate as wired only into image-generate-tool.ts's explicit model-override branch: trusted operator/system overrides are unchanged, no-override default/fallback skips the gate, and external/derived-untrusted/missing/invalid provenance with an explicit override may only use host-bound providers. Denial happens before any credential read and neither the policy input type nor the denial reason carries a credential value; other credential users are recorded as residual rather than claimed covered. No second credential policy was introduced and default provider, fallback and credential storage are untouched.\\\",\n  \\\"testsRun\\\": [\n    \\\"node harness/src/cli.mjs validate --spec harness/specs/tasks/harness-gap-credential-use-boundary.md --no-diff -> Spec is valid (exit 0)\\\",\n    \\\"node harness/src/cli.mjs validate --spec harness/specs/scenarios/gateway-backend-communication.md --no-diff -> Spec is valid (exit 0)\\\",\n    \\\"harness run --dry-run for the S05 task spec, reconstructed offline via harness/src/rules.mjs (changed-path ownership + backend-communication boundary scan) -> pass (dry-run), 0 failures, uncovered=[], residual=[]\\\",\n    \\\"tests/unit/provider-credential-use-boundary-ledger.test.ts executed against this working tree with a local vitest-compatible shim -> 4 passed, 0 failed\\\",\n    \\\"policy matrix against the working-tree provider-credential-use-policy.ts + shared/security/content-provenance.ts -> 18/18 assertions pass (no credential value in input type; denials restricted, credential-free reason; bound-provider allow; unbound/missing/blank deny)\\\",\n    \\\"credential scan over the 5 S05 files -> 0 hits\\\",\n    \\\"S05-SHA256SUMS readback -> 4/4 digests matched; s05-acceptance.json parses with driven_by=agent, realHuman=false, liveProvider=false\\\",\n    \\\"node scripts/check-no-bom.mjs -> ok (exit 0)\\\",\n    \\\"not runnable in this sandbox (no node_modules, no git repo; also absent at the pristine base checkout): pnpm test / typecheck:test / eslint / agent-dev gates, comms:replay + comms:compare, repo:test-coverage:check, check-repository-artifacts\\\"\n  ]\n}\n'@ -Encoding UTF8\nGet-Content \\\"D:\\\\tmp\\\\s05verify\\\\result.json\\\" -Raw\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
